    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with an emphasis on capitalizing on high-ceiling matchups against vulnerable arms. **James Wood** (78.42) stands as our premier start, boasting an elite xwOBA of 0.426 and a dream matchup against Bratt, whose 5.90 xERA provides a clear path to production. Similarly, **Austin Riley** (74.61) is primed for a massive outing; the favorable park factors (+16%) combined with a soft matchup against Brandon Young make him a must-start at 3B. We are also banking on **Brice Turang** (71.09) to provide necessary speed and contact, as his matchup against the contact-heavy Ryan Feltner (+19% SP skill advantage) elevates his floor significantly. **Corbin Carroll** (66.25) remains a high-priority play; while the matchup against Griffin is tougher, the slow delivery of the opposing starter provides the perfect environment for **Corbin Carroll** to weaponize his elite sprint speed and chase the stolen base points that are vital to our Roto standing.\n\nThe decision to bench **Josh Naylor** (53.40) was the most difficult pivot of the day, as he narrowly missed the cut despite a solid base projection. The optimizer favored the higher platoon-adjusted upside of **Vinnie Pasquantino** (63.01) against Mize, as **Josh Naylor** faces a significantly stiffer test in the 3.42 xERA of Nathan Eovaldi. Furthermore, several roster spots rely on pending lineup confirmations\u2014specifically **Brice Turang**, **Jose Caballero**, **Austin Riley**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Isaac Paredes**. If any of these players move down in the batting order or are held out of the starting nine, their scores will fluctuate, particularly for **Jose Caballero** (48.35), whose value is already capped by an assumed #8 spot against a 3.21 xERA arm. Investors should monitor the final lineups closely, as any negative shift in the order for **Tyler Soderstrom** or **Isaac Paredes** could necessitate a re-evaluation of the bench depth provided by **Seiya Suzuki** or **Henry Bolte**.",
